 /*
- * Pixel 3 (blueline) CPU clocks: ask SDM845's CPU frequency firmware
- * ("cpufreq-hw", one controller per cluster) for its highest regular
- * performance level. Without this the cores run at whatever level the
- * bootloader left. Same register interface as Linux's qcom-cpufreq-hw:
- * frequency table at +0x110 (40 rows of 32 bytes; 19.2 MHz * L_VAL, a
- * repeated frequency ends it, core count 1 marks turbo), requested index at
- * +0x920 (+4 per core with per-core DCVS). The firmware applies it within
- * its own voltage and thermal limits. Boot-arg bluecpufreq=0: leave as is.
+ * Pixel 3 (blueline) CPU clocks. SDM845's CPU and L3 clocks belong to the OSM
+ * (Operating State Manager) firmware, one register block per domain:
+ *   L3      0x17d41000  (downstream "osm_l3_base")
+ *   Silver  0x17d43000  cpu0-3 (mainline "freq-domain0", downstream "osm_pwrcl_base")
+ *   Gold    0x17d45800  cpu4-7 (mainline "freq-domain1", downstream "osm_perfcl_base")
+ * Register layout (Linux drivers/cpufreq/qcom-cpufreq-hw.c qcom_soc_data, and
+ * Google's crosshatch-4.9 drivers/clk/qcom/clk-cpu-osm.c, "v2" = SDM845 v2 silicon):
+ *   0x000 ENABLE          bit 0: firmware owns the domain
+ *   0x0bc DCVS_CTRL       bit 0: per-core requests (PERF_STATE + 4 * core)
+ *   0x110 FREQ_LUT        40 rows of 32 bytes: [31:30] source (0 = 300 MHz
+ *                         fixed clock), [18:16] max active cores (1 = turbo
+ *                         row), [7:0] L_VAL (x 19.2 MHz)
+ *   0x114 VOLT_LUT        [21:16] virtual corner, [11:0] open-loop mV
+ *   0x700 PSTATE_STATUS   [23:16] L_VAL the domain runs at now (downstream)
+ *   0x704 CURRENT_VOTE    [9:0] L_VAL ceiling after LMh limits (mainline throttle)
+ *   0x780/0x7d0           PERF_STATE / cycle counters on SDM845 v1 silicon
+ *   0x920 PERF_STATE      requested LUT index (+4 per core with per-core DCVS)
+ *   0x9c0 CYCLE_COUNTER   32-bit cycle count (+4 per core), v2
+ *
+ * Boot-args:
+ *   (none)          as 0106: put Silver and Gold at their top non-turbo level
+ *                   (bluecpufreq=0: leave the bootloader's levels).
+ *   bluecpu=1       read only: OSM enable, LUTs, status, limits, TSENS
+ *                   temperatures; time a dependent-add loop against CNTVCT
+ *                   on one Silver and one Gold core. Writes nothing.
+ *   bluecpu=2       bluecpu=1, then request bluecpu_silver=N / bluecpu_gold=N
+ *                   (default: top non-turbo level; bluecpu_turbo=1 allows the
+ *                   1-core turbo rows), wait, re-read, re-measure. Kept unless
+ *                   bluecpu_undo=1. bluecpu_l3=N also requests L3 level N.
+ *   bluecpu_scpu=N / bluecpu_gcpu=N   cores to measure on (default 1 / 4)
+ *   bluecpu_mxok=1  allow Silver above 1689.6 MHz / L3 above 1478.4 MHz when
+ *                   the domain is not already there (downstream votes the MX
+ *                   rail to TURBO for those; we do not).
+ *   bluecpu_lmh=1   also dump the first words of the LMh blocks (read only).
+ *   bluecpu_tsens=0 skip the TSENS reads.
  */
